      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 342 and 285. The GCD of two numbers is the largest positive integer that divides both numbers without leaving a remainder.\n\nLet's use the Euclidean algorithm to find the GCD of 342 and 285. The steps are as follows:\n\n1. Divide 342 by 285 and find the remainder.\n2. Replace 342 with 285 and 285 with the remainder from the previous step.\n3. Repeat the process until the remainder is 0. The non-zero remainder just before this last step will be the GCD.\n\nLet's implement this in Python:\n```python\ndef gcd(a, b):\n    while b:\n        a, b = b, a % b\n    return a\n\n# Given numbers\nnum1 = 342\nnum2 = 285\n\n# Calculate GCD\ngcd_result = gcd(num1, num2)\nprint(gcd_result)\n```\n```output\n57\n```\nThe greatest common divisor (GCD) of 342 and 285 is 57. Therefore, the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285 is \\(\\boxed{57}\\).",
